# DEFECT 083: an `@` cell holding a handle accepted against a header parameter
# of type `void *`, so C is handed the address of the program's own cell
# (panel 176's llm-ergonomist, reading the specification alone, 2026-09-23).
#
# SYMPTOM: `check` 0, `build` 0, and C freed a stack address: 134, three of
# three on Darwin, with `[C] eat got 0x16b9d24a8` where `make` had returned a
# heap address. The same over `record Box tag box` was refused by clang, `box **`
# against `box *`; `tag void` is `void **` against `void *`, which C converts
# without a word.
#
# CAUSE: `cli/pointee.hero` asked the header about width and sign for a
# NUMERIC `@` cell only; an opaque one — a handle, or a `ptr` — was asked
# nothing, and the probe hands both to C as `(void *)` on purpose (panel 103).
#
# FIX: an opaque `@` asks the header a different question, the DEPTH of its
# parameter: it must point at a pointer. `__builtin_classify_type` on the
# header's own pointee, in the same `_Static_assert` unit, at the author's
# line. The diagnostic is `ffi_parameter_type`, and its fix is a `guess`: drop
# the `@`, or the header is short by a star.
#
# `acquires drop` since 2026-09-24: the mark used to name `eat`, which
# `borrows` and so ends nothing, and `unread_releaser` reads every named
# releaser now, not only where some `extern` consumes the type.
extern "ffi-out-cell-on-a-handle-the-header-takes-by-value.h"
    record Mem tag void
    function make() -> Mem acquires drop
    function drop(p: Mem consumes)
    function eat(@p: Mem borrows)  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    m: Mem @= make()
    eat(@m)
    print("after")
